+// Orthros (OPENMW_ORTHROS_PRECOMPILE): every live Program, so that the ones not linked yet can be compiled before a
+// frame draws with them (osg::orthrosCompileUnlinkedPrograms, called by the engine while its loading screen is up and
+// at the first frame after it). Without it the first draw that applies a program compiles and links it, reading the
+// statuses synchronously: in a browser each status read waits for the GPU process to finish that compile and link
+// (100-380 ms for the big ones on SwiftShader), in the world's first frames.
+// A Program registers itself in its constructors and leaves first thing in its destructor, under the registry's
+// mutex. ~Program may run on another thread than the GL one (a postprocessing Shader userdata collected by Lua's GC on
+// the Lua thread, r14), so the compile pass holds the mutex while it uses a program: a Program being destroyed
+// elsewhere waits until the pass is done with it, and the pass passes over a program whose last reference is already
+// gone (referenceCount 0: its destructor is running or about to). The mutex is recursive and the pass walks a copy of
+// the list, checking each entry is still registered, so a Program made or destroyed on the GL thread inside a compile
+// can neither deadlock nor invalidate the walk. Order: by registration (a serial), the same from run to run.
